                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "Dk2WS",
                      "name": "whyBody",
                      "fill": "#5B6680",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The covering map sends card positions (fiber) to secret values (base). Genus constrains the AG code used for reconstruction: genus 0 gives exact threshold (Reed-Solomon), while genus > 0 forces a gap of up to 2g extra shares (Goppa bound). Larger groups need higher genus, so better anonymity costs more cooperation.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.4,
                      "fontFamily": "Inter",
                      "fontSize": 14,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
