                          "fill": "#0E2747",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "g = 3, R = 28,804 , |G| = 14,400",
                          "lineHeight": 1.5,
                          "textAlign": "center",
                          "fontFamily": "JetBrains Mono",
                          "fontSize": 22,
                          "fontWeight": "700"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "P5aL2",
                          "name": "t2",
                          "fill": "#0E2747",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": 429,
                          "content": "Local checks at write-time\nRiemann–Hurwitz: 2·3 + 2·14400 = 28804 + 2 ✓    \nRamification non-negative:  28804 ≥ 0 ✓          \nBranch points ≤ ramification:  holds  ✓       ",
                          "lineHeight": 1.5,
                          "fontFamily": "JetBrains Mono",
                          "fontSize": 16,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "gZmcn",
                          "name": "t3",
                          "fill": "#0E2747",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "Audit added a constraint we had not encoded\n  Aut bound:  |Aut(C)| ≤ 84(g−1)\n  forces  g ≥ 1 + 14400/84 ≈ 173.\n  No object with g = 3 exists.",
                          "lineHeight": 1.5,
                          "fontFamily": "JetBrains Mono",
                          "fontSize": 16,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "reMxt",
                      "name": "take",
                      "fill": "#5B6680",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": 529,
                      "content": "AI chose a 3-holed curve because Riemann–Hurwitz balanced exactly with 28,804 branch collisions and 14,400 symmetries, and took that balance as proof the curve exists. But for a single connected curve, an always-true property forbids 14,400 symmetries on fewer than 173 holes. The single-curve spec was hollow from the start. Allowing the curve to split into components restores low genus, but that is a separate framework refactor.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.4,
                      "textAlign": "center",
                      "fontFamily": "Inter",
                      "fontSize": 12,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
